<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to April 5.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to April 5.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar</p>
<p>Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June)</p>
<p>sugar crop to April 5 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week March 30-April 5</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,667,075 tns	184,151 tns    11.05 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,566,170 tns	188,056 tns    12.01 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,754,613 tns	195,076 tns    11.12 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to April 5</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    28,962,086 tns    3,130,983 tns    10.81 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    28,492,696 tns    3,062,923 tns    10.75 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    27,271,781 tns    2,888,656 tns    10.59 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 59 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 60 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 59 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
